# Krust

A WoW: Forever addon for client 1.60.1 (interface 16001). Copy the `Krust`
folder into the client's `Interface/AddOns` directory and reload the UI.

Krust displays current-level XP as a 25 x 4 grid (100 blocks, one per percent),
followed by an estimated time until the next level and the most recent XP gain.
When rested, the grid shifts to a light blue palette and shows a marker for the
rested-XP endpoint on the current level. Drag the display with the left mouse
button to move it.

Use `/krust show` and `/krust hide` to control visibility. Use `/krust quests`
to toggle the quest list window, and `/krust` to print current visibility and
usage. Position and visibility are remembered between sessions. An existing
enabled/disabled setting is migrated to the corresponding visibility.

The Quest List window is movable and can be resized by dragging its bottom-right
corner; its size is remembered. It groups active quests by quest color
(gray/green/yellow/red), then by zone. Each quest is shown as `[level] title`,
with objective progress listed below (for example `- 3/10`). Clicking a quest
row opens that quest in the default quest log UI.

XP continues to be tracked while the display is hidden. The latest gain shows
how many equally sized gains remain, rounded up. A gain that crosses one level
includes the XP spent finishing the previous level. At the level cap, Krust
reports the XP amount instead. If an update crosses more than one level, the
intermediate requirements are unavailable, so the gain cannot be calculated.
Routine XP reports are not sent to chat or to other players.

The ETA uses XP earned during up to the last 30 minutes divided by elapsed
in-game time, including idle time. It needs at least one minute of observation
and a measurable gain; without recent gains it becomes unavailable. It is an
estimate and will change with your XP rate. Tracking resets when entering the
world or when an XP change cannot be reliably measured; offline time is not
included.
